IMPORT prelude

-- United Nations Act 2001 (Singapore) -- the whole operative Act: the power to make sanctions regulations and its carve-outs for
-- MAS-supervised financial institutions and VCCs (s 2), immunity for non-performance caused by the Act (s 3), protection for acts
-- done under it (s 4), the penalty for breach of regulations and who is caught (s 5), citizens offending abroad and the bar on
-- extradition (s 6), and District Court jurisdiction (s 7).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 28/4/2023), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/UNA2001.txt, with amendments to Act 18 of 2022 (wef 28/04/2023) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. The Act is seven sections long, so nothing is
-- scoped out except: s 1 (short title); s 2(1)(a), (b) (what the regulations may provide for); s 2(6) (presenting regulations to
-- Parliament); s 2(7) (expenses); s 3(2) (the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959 is unaffected) beyond a comment. The regulations
-- themselves -- where every actual prohibition lives -- were not retrieved and are not encoded.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `United Nations Act 2001 -- sanctions`

§§ `2(1) -- the power to make regulations`

-- s 2(1): "if, under Article 41 of the Charter of the United Nations ... (being the Article which relates to measures not involving
-- the use of armed force), the Security Council of the United Nations calls upon the Government to apply any measures to give
-- effect to any decision of that Council, the Minister may, from time to time, make regulations that appear to the Minister to be
-- necessary or expedient for enabling those measures to be effectively applied".
GIVEN `the Security Council calls upon the Government` IS A BOOLEAN, `the call is under Article 41` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister thinks the regulations necessary or expedient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may make regulations` IF
    `the Security Council calls upon the Government` AND `the call is under Article 41` AND `the Minister thinks the regulations necessary or expedient`

§§ `2(2) to (4) -- financial institutions and VCCs are carved out`

-- s 2(2): the measures "do not apply to any financial institution ... to the extent that the financial institution ... is or may be
-- subject to the directions issued by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under section 15 of the Financial Services and Markets Act
-- 2022, or regulations made by [MAS] under section 192 ... for the purposes of section 15".  [Act 18 of 2022 wef 28/04/2023]
-- s 2(3): the same for "any VCC ... to the extent that the VCC ... is or may be subject to the directions or regulations made by
-- [MAS] under section 83 of the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018".
-- "is OR MAY BE subject": an institution that MAS could direct is outside the measures even if MAS has issued nothing. The "to the
-- extent that" qualifier is reduced here to a yes/no for the matter in question.
-- Note: s 2(1) opens "Subject to subsection (2)" only; the VCC carve-out in s 2(3) is not mentioned there, but is expressed in the
-- same words ("The measures to be applied under subsection (1) do not apply") and is given full effect here.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company`
    `a financial institution`
    `a VCC`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `is or may be subject to MAS directions or regulations on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the UN Act measures apply to the person` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a financial institution` THEN NOT `is or may be subject to MAS directions or regulations on the matter`
    WHEN `a VCC` THEN NOT `is or may be subject to MAS directions or regulations on the matter`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2(5) -- regulations override other written law, but not the Constitution`

-- s 2(5): "No regulation made under this Act is deemed to be invalid because it deals with any matter provided for by any written
-- law, or because of repugnancy to or inconsistency with any written law other than the Constitution."
-- INFERENCE: the subsection only removes the other grounds; that inconsistency with the Constitution CAN invalidate a regulation is
-- read from the words "other than the Constitution", not stated in this Act.
DECLARE OtherLaw IS ONE OF
    `another Act of Parliament`
    `other subsidiary legislation`
    `the Constitution`

GIVEN `the law` IS A OtherLaw
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `inconsistency with it can invalidate a UN Act regulation` IF
    CONSIDER `the law`
    WHEN `the Constitution` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- immunity from suit for non-performance`

-- s 3(1): "No action, suit or other legal proceedings shall lie against -- (a) any party to a contract for failing, neglecting or
-- refusing to carry out any act required by the contract; or (b) any person for failing, neglecting or refusing to carry out any
-- act under any written law, where the failure, neglect or refusal is SOLELY attributable to, or occasioned by, the provisions of this
-- Act or any regulations made under this Act."
-- s 3(2): "This section does not affect the operation of the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959." (Not modelled.)
DECLARE Duty IS ONE OF
    `an act required by a contract`
    `an act under a written law`
    `a duty of care in tort`

GIVEN `the duty` IS A Duty, `the failure is solely attributable to the Act or regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings for the failure are barred` IF
    `the failure is solely attributable to the Act or regulations`
    AND CONSIDER `the duty`
        WHEN `a duty of care in tort` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4 -- no personal liability for honest execution`

-- s 4: "No person shall be personally liable in respect of any act done by the person in the execution or purported execution of
-- this Act or any regulations made under this Act if the person did it in the honest belief that the person's duty under this Act
-- or any regulations ... required or entitled the person to do it."
GIVEN `done in execution or purported execution of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `honestly believed the duty required or entitled it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is protected from personal liability` IF
    `done in execution or purported execution of the Act` AND `honestly believed the duty required or entitled it`

§§ `5(1) -- who is liable, and the maximum penalty`

-- s 5(1): "Every person who commits, or attempts to commit, or does any act with intent to commit, or counsels, procures, aids,
-- abets, or incites any other person to commit, or conspires with any other person (whether in Singapore or elsewhere) to commit any
-- offence against any regulations made under this Act shall be liable on conviction -- (a) in the case of an individual, to a fine not
-- exceeding $500,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years or to both; or (b) in any other case, to a fine not
-- exceeding $1 million."  [4/2014]
-- Every listed form of participation carries the SAME maximum as the completed offence.
DECLARE Involvement IS ONE OF
    `committing`
    `attempting`
    `an act with intent to commit`
    `counselling`
    `procuring`
    `aiding`
    `abetting`
    `inciting`
    `conspiring`
    `knowing of it but taking no part`

GIVEN `the involvement` IS A Involvement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the involvement attracts s 5 liability` IF
    CONSIDER `the involvement`
    WHEN `knowing of it but taking no part` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 500000 ELSE 1000000

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 10 ELSE 0

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fine and imprisonment may both be imposed` IF `is an individual`

§§ `5(2) -- other written law, but no double punishment`

-- s 5(2): nothing prevents prosecution "under any other written law" for the same act, or a "higher or other" penalty under it, "but
-- no person shall be punished twice for the same offence".
GIVEN `already punished for the same offence under other written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be punished under the UN Act` IF NOT `already punished for the same offence under other written law`

§§ `6 -- citizens abroad, and the bar on extradition`

-- s 6(1): "The provisions of this Act have effect, in relation to citizens of Singapore, outside as well as within Singapore, and where
-- an offence ... is committed by a citizen of Singapore in any place outside Singapore, he or she may be dealt with in respect of that
-- offence as if it had been committed within Singapore."
-- For a NON-citizen acting outside Singapore, s 6 gives nothing; whether the Act reaches them is not decided here (but note the
-- conspiracy limb of s 5(1) runs "whether in Singapore or elsewhere"). The encoding answers only "does s 6 or territoriality reach it".
GIVEN `is a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `the conduct was in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be dealt with as if the offence were committed in Singapore` IF
    `the conduct was in Singapore` OR `is a Singapore citizen`

-- s 6(2): proceedings under s 6 that would bar later proceedings for the same offence, had it been committed in Singapore, are "a bar
-- to further proceedings against the person, under any written law ... relating to the extradition of persons, in respect of the same
-- offence outside Singapore".
GIVEN `s 6 proceedings would bar later proceedings had the offence been in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `extradition proceedings for the same offence are barred` IF
    `s 6 proceedings would bar later proceedings had the offence been in Singapore`

§§ `7 -- District Court jurisdiction`

-- s 7: "Despite any provision to the contrary in the Criminal Procedure Code 2010, a District Court has jurisdiction to try any offence
-- under this Act and has power to impose the full penalty or punishment in respect of the offence."  [9/2003]
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine a District Court may impose` MEANS `the maximum fine` `is an individual`

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years a District Court may impose` MEANS `the maximum imprisonment in years` `is an individual`
